{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"d99ecc181aa9f7ae","x":140,"y":-200,"width":720,"height":260,"type":"text","text":"In Ashk'lan, the golden city of river deltas, astromancers are feared almost more than the King's men. Once hired from among the eastern defector-magi, the astromancers taught the City literacy, mathematics, and astronomy. Most citizens have never seen a living astromancer—but they say that even the King himself doesn't know all their secrets. Their knowledge, after all, is forbidden to the uninitiated; this state of things cannot be changed, either by death or what comes after. The astromancers have now withdrawn from the court and rarely come to pay their respects. In their gaunt ivory towers, they create bookish learning on parchment, returning in their minds to the origins of the world. Their gods, they say, are hidden far beyond the realm of things..."},
		{"id":"dff8de7c9b662dcf","x":-464,"y":-360,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Main Mechanics: ???"}
